# Adding a New Entity — Full-Stack Checklist

Follow this order when adding any new entity to the Electro project.

## 1. JPA Entity (`model/`)
```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "my_entities")
public class MyEntity {
    @Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    @NotBlank
    private String name;

    private boolean active = true; // soft-delete flag when needed

    // relationships, getters/setters (or @Data with Lombok)
}
```

## 2. Repository (`repository/`)
```java
public interface MyEntityRepository extends JpaRepository<MyEntity, Long> {
    List<MyEntity> findByActiveTrue();
    // add custom @Query methods as needed
}
```

## 3. DTOs (`dto/request/` + `dto/response/`)
```java
// Request DTO — with validation
public class MyEntityRequest {
    @NotBlank private String name;
}

// Response DTO — plain POJO
public class MyEntityResponse {
    private Long id;
    private String name;
}
```

## 4. Service (`service/`)
- CRUD methods + business logic
- Inject repository, throw `ResourceNotFoundException` on missing records
- Map Entity ↔ DTO manually (no MapStruct)

## 5. Controllers
- **Public/designer**: `@RestController @RequestMapping("/api/designer/my-entities")` with `@PreAuthorize` or rely on SecurityConfig
- **Admin**: `@RestController @RequestMapping("/api/admin/my-entities")` for CRUD management

## 6. Data Initializer
- Add seed data to `DataInitializer.java` (always-run) or `TestDataInitializer.java` (test only)

## 7. Frontend API (`electro-frontend/src/api/api.js`)
```js
export const myEntityAPI = {
  getAll: () => api.get('/my-entities'),
  getById: (id) => api.get(`/my-entities/${id}`),
  create: (data) => api.post('/designer/my-entities', data),
  update: (id, data) => api.put(`/designer/my-entities/${id}`, data),
  delete: (id) => api.delete(`/designer/my-entities/${id}`),
};
```

## 8. Frontend Pages (`pages/`)
- List page with filter/sort/pagination using `UI/Pagination`
- Form page (create + edit) with controlled inputs → submit → navigate
- Add routes in `App.js` wrapped in `<ProtectedRoute>`

## Optional Steps
- **Excel import/export**: extend `ExcelDataExchangeService` + `AdminApplianceExcelController` pattern
- **File upload**: use `FileService` + `fileAPI` on frontend
